      "problem": "If $x-5=2,$ then $x=$",
      "worked_solution": "If we substitute $x=7$ into the given equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-5 & =2 \\\\ 7-5 & =2 \\\\ 2 & =2\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=7.$",
