      "problem": "If $\\frac{k}{8}=3,$ then $k=$",
      "worked_solution": "If we substitute $k=24$ into the given equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k}{8} & =3 \\\\ \\frac{24}{8} & =3 \\\\ 3 & =3\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $k=24.$",
